(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #90 — the control. Everything a buffer parameter already
 did right, kept right: an in-place byte write reaches the caller, growth
 that fits inside the first allocation was always visible, a fixed-size
 buffer still refuses to grow and sets the error flag, `Set` on a buffer
 parameter still copies bytes into the caller's buffer rather than rebinding
 the name, declaring a buffer of the parameter's own name inside the function
 names a buffer of that function's own and leaves the caller's alone, and
 growth at the top level is untouched by any of this. This file passes on
 both sides of the fix, which is the point of it.)

To 'poke' with a buffer called sink.
    Set byte 1 of sink to 65.

To 'pad a little' with a buffer called sink.
    a number called appended is 0.
    While appended is less than 20,
        append "0123456789" to sink,
        Set appended to appended add 1.

To 'overfill' with a buffer called sink.
    Set byte 9000 of sink to 65.

To 'refill' with a buffer called sink.
    Set sink to "much longer than the seed".

To 'shadow and grow' with a buffer called sink.
    a buffer called sink is "mine".
    a number called added is 0.
    While added is less than 600,
        append "0123456789" to sink,
        Set added to added add 1.
    Print "the callee's own buffer: {sink's size}".

a buffer called poked is "start".
'poke' of poked.
Print "an in-place write: {poked}".

a buffer called nudged is "start".
'pad a little' of nudged.
Print "growth inside the first allocation: {nudged's size}".

a buffer called fixed is 100 bytes.
'overfill' of fixed.
On error print "a fixed buffer still refuses".

a buffer called refilled is "start".
'refill' of refilled.
Print "Set through a parameter: {refilled}".

a buffer called shadowed is "start".
'shadow and grow' of shadowed.
Print "and the caller keeps its own: {shadowed's size}".

a buffer called topmost is "start".
a number called appended is 0.
While appended is less than 600,
    append "0123456789" to topmost,
    Set appended to appended add 1.
Print "grown at the top level: {topmost's size}".
